= Let the People Decide Everything

SPS proposes mandatory binding referendums for international treaties,
strategic sales and any welfare retrenchment. Parliament would frame the
question and then surrender the answer.

Constitutional restraint: **[+ constitutional_restraint +]/100**. Anti-system
trust: **[+ anti_system_trust +]/100**.

- @populist_referendum_mandate
- @populist_referendum_citizens
- @populist_referendum_refuse

@populist_referendum_mandate
title: Constitutionalise the mandatory referendums
subtitle: SPS and anti-system trust surge; representative government and coalition control weaken.
on-arrival: social_patriot_support += 10; social_patriot_strength += 4; social_patriot_dissent -= 9; sld_populist_media_salience += 9; sld_populist_factional_capture += 6; anti_system_trust += 8; rural_support += 5; constitutional_restraint -= 7; institutional_trust -= 5; government_delivery -= 3; ko_relation -= 7; p2050_relation -= 6; progressives_dissent += 5; government_coalition_dissent += 8; early_election_risk += 4; news_headline = "Government proposes mandatory referendums on treaties, welfare and strategic assets"

Every future cabinet acquires a veto player with millions of names and no duty
to reconcile the answers.

